theme_override_constants/line_spacing = 8
theme_override_font_sizes/font_size = 28
text = "By the year 2300, humanity had exhausted all the resources of Earth. They started to look for a suitable planet to move to. Their search led them to Aetheron-12, a fertile planet populated by sentient, peace-loving creatures that resembled Earth’s octopi.

The humans’ first contact was peaceful. They learned that the creatures called themselves the Cephari. Soon, they learned that the Cephari were not a threat, and they began trading with the Cephari. Humans established trading outposts on Aetheron-12.

But as the situation on Earth became dire, what was initially a benevolent interaction turned into something more sinister. Trading outposts grew in area and quantity. Soon, the humans’ demands became stronger. They wanted more land and for local slaves to be sold to them. As the Cephari realized the threat, the humans unleashed a war against them.

The octopi found one pivotal weakness in humans. They could stall a human soldier by showing them a special type of video called “brainrot.” The mechanism behind this weakness was unknown, but this became the Cephari’s strongest weapon against humanity. To power their defenses and destroy the invaders, the Cephari needed to gather enough Scrollium.

The battle for Aetheron-12 began…"
horizontal_alignment = 1
autowrap_mode = 3

